-- title:
--   A nonempty rational polyhedron over any ordered field contains a rational point.
-- statement:
--   A nonempty rational polyhedron over any ordered field contains a rational point.
--   The height bound uses only the number of variables and the maximum row-entry
--   height, so it applies even when the number of inequalities is exponential.
--
--   This lemma is part of OpenAI's machine-checked proof that rational linear programs can be solved by a strongly polynomial algorithm on a real-number RAM (Smale's ninth problem). It is used in the proof of `OAI.Optimization.LinearProgramming.Compression.exists_small_rat_feasible_with_fixed`.
